:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300956}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c6c2c622-589c-57e8-8e2b-f4a0e13ed191" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300956} :answer-field/id #uuid "ba198b2a-625a-56f7-832e-5a614a281fa8" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301838}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7a41944b-5b17-58c0-b340-9129937f3ee2" :question/math-academy-id "q-326259" :question/problem "Given that a curve is defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=2t-7,\\,y=3-t,\\,t\\le 4.\n$$\n\nDetermine the ranges of $x$ and $y.$\n\n$x$\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}$,\\,y$\n{{field-3}}{{field-4}}" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider each variable in turn.\n\n- To find the range of $x,$ note that $x=2t-7\\le 1$ for all $t\\le 4.$ Consequently, the range of $x$ is\n\n$$\nx\\le 1.\n$$\n\n- To find the range of $y,$ note that $y=3-t\\ge -1$ for all $t\\le 4.$ Consequently, the range of $y$ is\n\n$$\ny\\ge -1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302278 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "030a64cf-fc76-5914-85f8-c09965785117" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299945}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "030a64cf-fc76-5914-85f8-c09965785117" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299945} :answer-field/id #uuid "2fdfe631-b001-5c4d-9acb-599647a7f69e" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301375} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aec764c0-a442-501c-b10b-4d44