b/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301824} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "72c185d8-fa43-53bf-b4a9-350d066cb586" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300533}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "72c185d8-fa43-53bf-b4a9-350d066cb586" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300533} :answer-field/id #uuid "f117f64d-057e-5a62-a0f1-b60e45fc5a11" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301995}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "519df9e7-1dc6-5ad7-93ad-7804c67f997d" :question/math-academy-id "q-327884" :question/problem "Given that a curve is defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{1}{3}-\\frac{4}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=\\frac{5}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -\\frac{7}{3},\\,0\\le \\theta <2\\pi ,\n$$\n\nwhat are the ranges of $x$ and $y?$\n\nThe range of $x$ is \n{{field-1}}\n$\\le x$\n{{field-2}}{{field-3}}.\n\nThe range of $y$ is \n{{field-4}}\n$\\le y$\n{{field-5}}{{field-6}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's consider each variable in turn.\n\n- To find the range of $x,$ notice that for $0\\le \\theta <2\\pi ,$ \nwe have $-1\\le \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\le 1.$ Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & \\le \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\le 1 \\\\ \\frac{4}{3} & \\text{ }\\ge -\\frac{4}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\text{ }\\ge -\\frac{4}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{4}{3} & \\le -\\frac{4}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\le \\frac{4}{3} \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}-\\frac{4}{3} & \\le \\frac{1}{3}-\\frac{4}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\le \\frac{1}{3}+\\frac{4}{3} \\\\ -1 & \\le x\\le \\frac{5}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can conclude that $-1\\le x\\le \\frac{5}{3}.$\n\n- To find the range of $y,$ notice that for $0\\le \\theta <2\\pi ,$ \nwe have $-1\\le \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\le 1.$ Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & \\le \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\le 1 \\\\ -\\frac{5}{2} & \\le \\frac{5}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\le \\frac{5}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{5}{2}-\\frac{7}{3} & \\le \\frac{5}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -\\frac{7}{3}\\le \\frac{5}{2}-\\frac{7}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{29}{6} & \\le y\\le \\frac{1}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can conclude that $-\\frac{29}{6}\\le y\\le \\frac{1}{6}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314703 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2208ccc5-5934-51e2-b52d-8ff31bed4e36" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{1+4{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312232} {:answer/id #uuid "65d3df9b-2970-5299-ab99-547382b11901" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{1+{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312777} {:answer/id #uuid "7ce9c1bd-fb44-5c82-b8e8-5b81f7969c0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{1+{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312977} {:answer/id #uuid "a95d6aed-c1ec-5c63-b9a8-8a0ba8e816ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{1+{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313302} {:answer/id #uuid "b5c14440-88e2-525d-85e7-2db79078355d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡2t-{sin}^{2}⁡2t+{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313388}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a95d6aed-c1ec-5c63-b9a8-8a0ba8e816ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{1+{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313302} :answer-field/id #uuid "9762ce0e-0f2a-5c5c-ad7d-6b8b6bc424c7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314419}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "732ad1b9-5772-5700-8754-f590c45d555d" :question/math-academy-id "q-33857" :question/problem "Which integral  expression gives the arc length of the curve $f(t)=⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t,\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t,{t}^{2}⟩$\nfrom  $t=0$ to $t=1?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find ${f}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{f}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t,\\,-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t,\\,2t⟩ \\\\ ‖{f}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)^{2}+(-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t)^{2}+(2t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{cos}^{2}⁡2t+4{sin}^{2}⁡2t+4{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4({cos}^{2}⁡2t+{sin}^{2}⁡2t+{t}^{2})} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{1+{t}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}‖{f}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t={\\int }_{0}^{1}2\\sqrt{1+{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314997 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "db185f31-d898-509f-b9c4-a2881a9060fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-28(1-7x)^3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313696} {:answer/id #uuid "0367ff3f-be48-44c0-9200-bace643c1760" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-28\\left(1-7x\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186576513}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "db185f31-d898-509f-b9c4-a2881a9060fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-28(1-7x)^3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313696} :answer-field/id #uuid "36ad8472-0eaf-547f-a51d-d9fd88b94c6d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314156}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "45dae178-5aad-56cb-99e8-4cae2859e574" :question/math-academy-id "q-340690" :question/problem "Find $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}$ when $f(x)=(1-7x)^{4}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $f(x)$ as a composite function:\n\n$$\nf={g}^{4},\\,g=1-7x\n$$\n\nThe chain rule states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}=4{g}^{3},\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}=-7.\n$$\n\nFinally, multiplying the two together and substituting for $g$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =4{g}^{3}\\cdot (-7) \\\\  & =-28(1-7x)^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317301 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9dddace1-6902-5bd8-8d9c-4f8e9ee4c695" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316001}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9dddace1-6902-5bd8-8d9c-4f8e9ee4c695" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316001} :answer-field/id #uuid "fb310ac7-3d59-5c34-90b1-fa1d08886eef" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317143}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f5911b4d-cb67-58a7-a1eb-0368289d94d7" :question/math-academy-id "q-342630" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)={({x}^{2}+2x+1)}^{2},$ the slope at the point $(0,1)$ is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "To find the slope at a given point, we have to find $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point.\n\nWe use the chain rule to find $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\nFirst, we express $f(x)$ as a composite function:\n\n$$\nf={g}^{2},\\,g={x}^{2}+2x+1\n$$\n\nThe chain rule states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}=2g,\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}=2x+2.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the two together and substituting for $g$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =2g\\cdot (2x+2) \\\\  & =2({x}^{2}+2x+1)(2x+2).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent line at the point where $x=0$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=0} & =[2({x}^{2}+2x+1)(2x+2){]}_{x=0} \\\\  & =2((0{)}^{2}+2\\cdot (0)+1)(2\\cdot (0)+2) \\\\  & =2(1)(2) \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317308 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "afdc11cd-82dd-5c6f-bcb3-29722512bae8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-96" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316117}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "afdc11cd-82dd-5c6f-bcb3-29722512bae8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-96" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316117} :answer-field/id #uuid "466922a0-7e46-579f-8acd-8a627c38b832" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316705}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4d9eda9c-9861-5891-97dc-ba4b870f7db4" :question/math-academy-id "q-342663" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)={(3x+1)}^{4},$ the slope at the point $(-1,16)$ is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "To find the slope at a given point, we have to find $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point.\n\nWe use chain rule to find $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\nFirst, we express $f(x)$ as a composite function:\n\n$$\nf={g}^{4},\\,g=3x+1\n$$\n\nThe chain rule states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}=4{g}^{3},\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}=3.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the two together and substituting for $g$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =4{g}^{3}\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =12(3x+1{)}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent line at the point where $x=-1$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=-1} & =[12(3x+1{)}^{3}{]}_{x=-1} \\\\  & =12(3\\cdot (-1)+1{)}^{3} \\\\  & =12(-2{)}^{3} \\\\  & =-96.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317312 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c3cdb155-0bd1-58bc-961e-1bfa7707dad6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x-3}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-6x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316217} {:answer/id #uuid "6547e4e5-5934-4e34-acb1-3afb5ae5bf10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\left(x-3\\right)}{\\sqrt{x^2-6x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186576552}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c3cdb155-0bd1-58bc-961e-1bfa7707dad6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x-3}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-6x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316217} :answer-field/id #uuid "fd768cbb-f716-59e5-acc7-6f058b68d4ef" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317150}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "1f8a23e9-b484-592c-83ed-60ed3cc8b897" :question/math-academy-id "q-342680" :question/problem "Given that $y=\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-6x}$, find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We use the chain rule in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nLet $u={x}^{2}-6x.$ Then $y=\\sqrt{u}.$ Differentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{u}},\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2x-6.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the two together gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{u}}\\cdot (2x-6) \\\\  & =\\frac{2(x-3)}{2\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-6x}} \\\\  & =\\frac{x-3}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-6x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317313 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8316ace3-a7b2-57fb-a2e0-d20a2908d622" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2\\sqrt{3x+6}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315844}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8316ace3-a7b2-57fb-a2e0-d20a2908d622" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2\\sqrt{3x+6}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315844} :answer-field/id #uuid "b7c696cc-7f33-5839-8d2a-38d27e70f63c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316978}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c93d262c-d38e-53b1-ba9c-9af520b2e82c" :question/math-academy-id "q-342683" :question/problem "Given that $y=\\sqrt{3x+6}$, find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We use the chain rule in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nLet $u=3x+6.$ Then $y=\\sqrt{u}.$ Differentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{u}},\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=3.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the two together gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{u}}\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2\\sqrt{3x+6}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317321 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ea0b074e-9124-53da-b940-4a0beab23775" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{2\\sqrt{(5x+1)^{3}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316419} {:answer/id #uuid "4abe05c3-0f06-52ad-8909-cbe4491128f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{2(5x+1)^{3/2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524509} {:answer/id #uuid "41e5e3a5-9d36-48a7-bc0f-19bdd775286f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186576469} {:answer/id #uuid "9562bb93-b2ba-493b-b623-c0b002ef200c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac52" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186576470} {:answer/id #uuid "79ba6767-590d-47b0-8fdc-a86a2e93a19a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac52\\left(\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186576471} {:answer/id #uuid "24c1f001-0d0c-4e27-9152-530789816a6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac52\\left(5x\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186576472} {:answer/id #uuid "f3bdc8ea-ee8f-4bfc-8c2b-63128b70751d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac52\\left(5x+1\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186576473}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4abe05c3-0f06-52ad-8909-cbe4491128f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{2(5x+1)^{3/2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524509} :answer-field/id #uuid "cae0bf8f-009f-5cd9-a958-5250470d215a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317025}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "65a56fb3-c803-55e2-851b-d52f4cc805e8" :question/math-academy-id "q-342764" :question/problem "Find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for $y=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5x+1}}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We use the chain rule in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nLet $u=5x+1.$ Then $y=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}}={u}^{-1/2}.$ Differentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}=-\\frac{1}{2}{u}^{-3/2}=-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{{u}^{3}}},\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=5.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the two together gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{{u}^{3}}}\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{2\\sqrt{{u}^{3}}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{2\\sqrt{(5x+1)^{3}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317326 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22c57943-65ff-5d5d-81f8-1002a59bb417" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{18}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315311}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "22c57943-65ff-5d5d-81f8-1002a59bb417" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{18}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315311} :answer-field/id #uuid "4e7bce52-e2d7-50a5-a44d-84c8a8cc1d7d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316728}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "febc6c25-71ff-51d9-b851-6f19e65ebcd1" :question/math-academy-id "q-342802" :question/problem "The slope of the tangent to the curve $y=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3{x}^{2}+12x}}$ at the point where $x=2$ is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "To find the slope at a given point, we have to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point.\n\nWe use the chain rule in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nLet $u=3{x}^{2}+12x.$ Then $y=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}}={u}^{-1/2}.$ Differentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}=-\\frac{1}{2}{u}^{-3/2}=-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{{u}^{3}}},\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=6x+12.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the two together gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{{u}^{3}}}\\cdot (6x+12) \\\\  & =-\\frac{6x+12}{2\\sqrt{(3{x}^{2}+12x{)}^{3}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $x=2,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=2} & ={\\left(-\\frac{6x+12}{2\\sqrt{(3{x}^{2}+12x{)}^{3}}}\\right)|}_{x=2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{6(2)+12}{2\\sqrt{(3(2{)}^{2}+12(2){)}^{3}}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{24}{2\\sqrt{{36}^{3}}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{18}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317327 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bc8b5aee-000a-5a8d-818f-e20c5debd3ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20(4x+3)^{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316184} {:answer/id #uuid "7c419ad2-83cf-57c7-b5a2-d7c1c6a8cf6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20(4x+3)^4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541677}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7c419ad2-83cf-57c7-b5a2-d7c1c6a8cf6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20(4x+3)^4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541677} :answer-field/id #uuid "625a79d7-54d7-570b-aa7c-729d582ac660" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316778}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9ebc59fe-5ccc-59b1-9757-9c760459c2ae" :question/math-academy-id "q-342804" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)={(4x+3)}^{5},$ find ${f}^{′}(x).$\n\n${f}^{′}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $g(x)=4x+3$ and $f(g(x))=g(x)^{5}.$ \n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(g(x)) & =({g}^{5})^{′}=5{g}^{4}, \\\\ {g}^{′}(x) & =(4x+3)^{′}=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the chain rule, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={f}^{′}(g(x))\\cdot {g}^{′}(x) \\\\  & =5{g}^{4}\\cdot (4) \\\\  & =20(4x+3)^{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317333 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8817f05b-018c-5853-b6cc-e00880617a94" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5{x}^{4}-16{x}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315880}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8817f05b-018c-5853-b6cc-e00880617a94" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5{x}^{4}-16{x}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315880} :answer-field/id #uuid "e5ab2d60-fecd-56b2-a6fc-370a03381af0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317093}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "2fb4db78-694f-5845-af11-624db7bcff81" :question/math-academy-id "q-342875" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)={({x}^{5}-4{x}^{4})}^{2},$ find ${f}^{′}(x).$\n\n${f}^{′}(x)=2({x}^{5}-4{x}^{4})($\n{{field-1}}\n$)$" :question/worked-solution "Let $g(x)={x}^{5}-4{x}^{4}$ and $f(g(x))=g(x)^{2}.$ \n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(g(x)) & =({g}^{2})^{′}=2g, \\\\ {g}^{′}(x) & =({x}^{5}-4{x}^{4})^{′}=5{x}^{4}-16{x}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the chain rule, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={f}^{′}(g(x))\\cdot {g}^{′}(x) \\\\  & =2g\\cdot (5{x}^{4}-16{x}^{3}) \\\\  & =2({x}^{5}-4{x}^{4})(\\,5{x}^{4}-16{x}^{3}\\,).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317335 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "54037730-2600-58cb-b40d-648fd184a076" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2\\sqrt{5x-4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315600}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "54037730-2600-58cb-b40d-648fd184a076" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2\\sqrt{5x-4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315600} :answer-field/id #uuid "0f9abe6a-bb3b-59b2-9f07-73fdde4dcc36" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316583}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "6a140a75-4d09-557b-baa7-d7202838dd2f" :question/math-academy-id "q-342883" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=\\sqrt{5x-4},$ find ${f}^{′}(x).$\n\n${f}^{′}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $g(x)=5x-4$ and $f(g(x))=\\sqrt{g(x)}.$ \n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(g(x)) & ={(\\sqrt{g})}^{′}=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{g}}, \\\\ {g}^{′}(x) & =(5x-4)^{′}=5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the chain rule, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={f}^{′}(g(x))\\cdot {g}^{′}(x) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{g}}\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2\\sqrt{5x-4}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317336 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d665e027-6ab2-5ec3-82b7-84f4dddc219b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x-4{x}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316315}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d665e027-6ab2-5ec3-82b7-84f4dddc219b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x-4{x}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316315} :answer-field/id #uuid "e1297ade-d13c-5373-bff2-2ee35469ee63" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317084}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "49fe03e2-8c48-5c16-b76a-8505b327ec2d" :question/math-academy-id "q-342891" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2{x}^{4}-{x}^{2}+5}},$ find ${f}^{′}(x).$\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{(2{x}^{4}-{x}^{2}+5{)}^{3}}}(\n$$\n{{field-1}}\n$)$" :question/worked-solution "Let $g(x)=2{x}^{4}-{x}^{2}+5$ and $f(g(x))=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{g(x)}}.$ \n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(g(x)) & ={\\left(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{g}}\\right)}^{′}=-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{{g}^{3}}}, \\\\ {g}^{′}(x) & =(2{x}^{4}-{x}^{2}+5{)}^{′}=8{x}^{3}-2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the chain rule, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={f}^{′}(g(x))\\cdot {g}^{′}(x) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{{g}^{3}}}\\cdot (8{x}^{3}-2x) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{(2{x}^{4}-{x}^{2}+5{)}^{3}}}(\\,x-4{x}^{3}\\,).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317337 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9e15c4f3-e0aa-5296-8996-2def04133195" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6x+11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316002}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9e15c4f3-e0aa-5296-8996-2def04133195" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6x+11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316002} :answer-field/id #uuid "adb706a4-b97c-5d9a-a3d9-b9ec8f4ae7e2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316955}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "f16d8b27-8720-58fb-ad21-d69be0217bc6" :question/math-academy-id "q-342910" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=(3-2x{)}^{3},$ the equation of the tangent at the point $(2,-1)$ is\n\n$y=$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "To find the slope at a given point, we have to find $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point.\n\nWe use the chain rule to find $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\nFirst, we express $f(x)$ as a composite function:\n\n$$\nf={g}^{3},\\,g=3-2x\n$$\n\nThe chain rule states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}=3{g}^{2},\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}=-2.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the two together and substituting for $g$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =3{g}^{2}\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =-6(3-2x{)}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent line at the point where $x=2$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=2} & =(-6{(3-2x)}^{2}){|}_{x=2} \\\\  & =-6{(3-2(2))}^{2} \\\\  & =-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the slope of the tangent line at the point $(2,-1)$ is $m=-6.$ Now, we find the equation of the tangent at that point:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y+1 & =-6\\cdot (x-2) \\\\ y & =-6x+12-1 \\\\ y & =-6x+11\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
